  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Crazy Eights. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Crazy Eights is a popular shedding card game, especially beloved by children. The objective is simple: be the first player to discard all your cards. Players take turns playing cards to a central discard pile, matching either the rank or suit of the top card. The eponymous "crazy" 8s are wild cards that can be played on anything and allow the player to change the suit.',
    objective: 'Score by emptying your Ligretto stack and playing cards faster than opponents.',
    gameplay: 'Players act simultaneously, playing cards from their rows, hands, and Ligretto stacks onto shared ascending color piles. When a player empties their Ligretto stack, the round stops and cards played are scored against cards left.',
    keyRules: [
      'There are no turns; play is simultaneous.',
      'Cards are played by color in ascending sequence.',
      'The round ends immediately when a player empties their Ligretto stack.',
    ],
